Here is the short, clean, correct method to create an offline Kea tar.gz package from inside an Ubuntu build container, so you can later install it on another EC2 VM without internet.

⸻

✅ FASTEST WAY to build an offline Kea tar.gz

Inside Ubuntu build container
	1.	Install build dependencies
(needs internet only in the build container)

apt-get update
apt-get install -y build-essential automake libtool pkg-config \
  libssl-dev libboost-all-dev liblog4cplus-dev libpq-dev \
  libmysqlclient-dev libcurl4-openssl-dev flex bison

	2.	Download Kea source

wget https://ftp.isc.org/isc/kea/3.0.0/kea-3.0.0.tar.gz
tar -xzf kea-3.0.0.tar.gz
cd kea-3.0.0

	3.	Configure + build

./configure
make -j$(nproc)
make install DESTDIR=/tmp/kea-offline

This installs all compiled files into:

/tmp/kea-offline/usr/local/

	4.	Create your offline tar.gz

cd /tmp
tar -czf kea-offline.tar.gz kea-offline

Now you have:

/tmp/kea-offline.tar.gz

✔ contains binaries
✔ contains libs
✔ contains hooks
✔ ready to install anywhere without internet

⸻

🔧 Install on another offline EC2 VM

Copy the tarball to the server, then run:

tar -xzf kea-offline.tar.gz -C /

Because you used DESTDIR, the tarball expands exactly into the correct paths:

/usr/local/sbin/kea-dhcp4
/usr/local/lib/
...

No building, no dependencies, no internet.

⸻

✔ Why this is the best method
	•	No need to rebuild on the EC2 VM
	•	No need to install build tools there
	•	Exactly matches your compiled Kea version
	•	Fastest possible offline deployment

